[Music]  who are you  the story of chiang chi  was actually very personal  i wanted to look at what superhero could  be  what it would mean to me  to be able to add not only one character  shanghi  but to add a whole cornucopia of asian  faces that are representing something  i've never really seen before  what happened to your shirt  i never thought in my wildest dreams  that i would be here  i was pretty much the biggest marvel fan  that you could possibly imagine to be  the first lead asian superhero in the  mcu this is every kid's dream  for many of us who grew up in the west  whose parents immigrated you know we  never really saw ourselves on screen  meaningfully chiang chi will be an  important piece of that conversation i'm  chinese american i was raised here i was  interested in exploring what that story  could be like it's an amazing  opportunity to write a little bit more  of my experience  everyone on this movie they care about  the story whether it's the language the  symbology everything was done with care  with research we all bonded because it's  just such an important film  you were meant for greatness  every time i talk to my parents they  always lead with the same question did  you work with tony leung today and did  you work with michelle yo today tony and  michelle are  as legendary as you can get  you are a product of all who came before  you the good and the bad every marvel  superhero has their own story and  everyone is so different when your  storytelling is good it transcends the  culture because at the end of the day  we're telling a story about love about  family i hope this movie is something  that anybody will feel connected to  it's time to show them who i really am  [Applause]  [Music]

